From ea58ea6b2662fae763ed4bb28fe25e4d7ff4c71a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 16:01:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 31/63] glm cuda: the follower's step in one broadcast, rank
 0's keep on its next step, a window's greedy picks in one gather

No arithmetic changes; the steps' GPU work runs in the same order on every rank.

- Every step's first broadcast is 384 bytes, the header and up to 80 ids (a decode step's all): one host
  round trip on the other ranks instead of two. Longer steps follow with the whole message.
- Rank 0 commits a keep at once and sends it on its next verify, block or draft step of the same slot
  (Link.keep_flag); any other step, or a second keep, sends it alone as before.
- A follower's verify and shared steps join their draws' gathers and skip the sync and read
  (Engine.discard_draws): rank 0 alone reads those tokens.
- greedyRows: a window's rows each take their top-1 launch, then one all-gather, one sync and one read for
  all of them (each row picked by chance.pick as before). Also carries TF_GLM_MOE_FUSE's engine switch.

